%requires qore >= 2.0
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesReplUi

# Optional magic module for rich file type detection in FileBrowserWidget
# magic_file_info() was added in magic 2.0
%try-module magic >= 2.0
%define NO_MAGIC
%endtry

%modern

module NcursesUi {
    version = "1.0";
    desc = "Ncurses terminal UI toolkit";
    author = "Qore Technologies, s.r.o.";
    license = "MIT";
}

/** @mainpage NcursesUi Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section ncursesuiintro NcursesUi Module Introduction

    The NcursesUi module provides a complete terminal UI toolkit built on the
    ncurses binary module. It provides:

    - A widget tree with parent-child relationships and focus management
    - Layout managers (@ref NcursesUi::BoxLayout "BoxLayout", @ref NcursesUi::SplitLayout "SplitLayout")
    - Unicode-aware terminal text measurement, clipping, and padding
    - Indexed scrollable content with retention and stable source identities
    - Multiline editing, atomic paste, selection, undo and searchable draft history
    - Searchable transcripts with logical blocks, tail following and link callbacks
    - Typed event dispatch with modal stack and mouse hit-testing
    - Standard UI components (list, text input, dialog, menu bar, status bar,
      file browser, combo box, checkbox, radio group, table)
    - Typed forms, labels/help/errors, buttons and described choices with custom responses
    - Tree/key-value inspectors and searchable read-only code with syntax styling
    - @ref NcursesUi::Application "Application" encapsulates the event loop
    - Headless testing with @ref Qore::Ncurses::TestTerminal "TestTerminal"

    To use the module:
    @code{.py}
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi
    @endcode

    @section ncursesui_arch Architecture

    @subsection ncursesui_tree Widget Tree

    Every UI element is a @ref NcursesUi::Widget "Widget". Widgets form a tree
    via parent-child relationships. Each widget has:
    - A geometry rectangle (@ref NcursesUi::Rect "Rect") describing its position and size
    - A focus state (@ref NcursesUi::Widget::hasFocus() "hasFocus()" / @ref NcursesUi::Widget::setFocused() "setFocused()")
    - Local invalidation, with descendant dirtiness observed by ancestors
    - @ref NcursesUi::Widget::processEvent() "processEvent()" for handling input events

    Pass the root to @ref NcursesUi::Application::setRoot() "Application::setRoot()", then call
    @ref NcursesUi::Application::run() "Application::run()" to manage the event loop and drawing.

    @subsection ncursesui_layouts Layout Managers

    Layout managers are separate objects that position the children of a container widget:

    - @ref NcursesUi::BoxLayout "BoxLayout": arranges children in a row (horizontal)
      or column (vertical), distributing space based on each child's
      @ref NcursesUi::SizePolicy "SizePolicy"
    - @ref NcursesUi::SplitLayout "SplitLayout": divides space between exactly two
      visible children using a ratio or fixed size in terminal rows/columns

    Use @ref NcursesUi::Widget::addChild() "Widget::addChild()" to populate the container,
    then @ref NcursesUi::BoxLayout::apply() "BoxLayout::apply()" or
    @ref NcursesUi::SplitLayout::apply() "SplitLayout::apply()" to calculate child geometry.
    Configure a split with @ref NcursesUi::SplitLayout::setSplitRatio() "SplitLayout::setSplitRatio()"
    or @ref NcursesUi::SplitLayout::setFixedSize() "SplitLayout::setFixedSize()".
    For a complete list/status layout example, see @ref ncurses_ui_app "List and Status Application".

    Vertical box layouts measure wrapped controls with getPreferredSizeForWidth()
    before allocating rows. TextEditorWidget uses this to request its bounded
    automatic height; other layouts may call the same measurement hook.

    Widget trees, input buffers, and focus managers belong to the application's
    UI thread. Update them from that thread and its callbacks; do not mutate
    the same UI state concurrently from worker threads. Binary terminal calls
    retain the ncurses session's locking discipline.

    Widget frames and mouse events always use absolute screen coordinates.
    Custom drawing calls @ref NcursesUi::Widget::drawContentRect() "drawContentRect(window)"
    to convert to the target window. Tree drawing clips overflowing children to
    ancestor content and window bounds, including nested panels. Zero-area
    widgets release rendering resources without painting. Fixed/minimum box
    requests are truncated in order when the parent is too small; expanding
    controls receive their minima before sharing the remaining space.

    Active panels, dialogs, and anchored popups reflow on terminal resize.
    Dialogs keep the focused action reachable with Tab on narrow terminals;
    Up/Down and PageUp/PageDown scroll long, wrapped messages. Choice controls
    use their drawable height for scrolling, keyboard navigation, and mouse input.
    Menus skip disabled entries and separators, including all-disabled menus.

    @subsection ncursesui_focus Focus Management

    @ref NcursesUi::FocusManager "FocusManager" traverses the widget tree to
    move focus between widgets. Widgets declare whether they accept focus via
    @ref NcursesUi::Widget::setFocusable() "setFocusable()". Tab / Shift+Tab cycle through focusable widgets using
    the @ref NcursesUi::FocusDirection "FocusDirection" enum. Non-focusable
    containers do not interrupt routing to descendants. Hidden and disabled
    subtrees are excluded; detaching or reparenting a subtree clears its focus.
    Use @ref NcursesUi::FocusManager::setFocus() "setFocus()" for application
    focus changes. Callbacks may inspect focus but cannot initiate a nested
    focus or modal-stack transition; callback failures leave no stale owner.
    This guard also covers callbacks from direct focus changes and subtree
    hide, disable, and detach operations. Cleanup may release focus, but a focus
    callback cannot acquire focus on another widget.

    @subsection ncursesui_events Event Dispatch

    @ref NcursesUi::EventDispatcher "EventDispatcher" routes input events:
    - Explicit global handlers run first, including while a modal is active.
    - Keyboard events go to the focused descendant and bubble through its ancestors.
    - A primary mouse click focuses the eligible hit target; misses and wheel events
      never fall through to an unrelated focused control.
    - Composites can override
      @ref NcursesUi::Widget::handlesChildMouseEvents() "handlesChildMouseEvents()"
      to receive screen-coordinate mouse events before their children, and
      @ref NcursesUi::Widget::mouseFocusTarget() "mouseFocusTarget()" to select
      the appropriate child for primary activation. File-browser preview
      navigation uses this contract; child frames and events retain screen coordinates.
    - A modal captures all remaining input. Tab/Shift+Tab stay in its focus scope;
      controls with internal Tab navigation handle the key first.
    - @ref NcursesUi::Application::pushPopup() "pushPopup()" opts into outside-click
      dismissal and click-through. Ordinary modals never pass outside clicks through.
    - Popping nested scopes restores the previous eligible focus. Text editors show
      a caret, and closing the last modal restores the prior cursor visibility.

    @subsection ncursesui_panels Panels and Modals

    @ref NcursesUi::PanelWidget "PanelWidget" wraps an ncurses Panel to create
    a floating overlay. It manages its own window and draws independently of
    the main widget tree. Push a PanelWidget as a modal via
    @ref NcursesUi::Application::pushModal() "Application::pushModal()" to capture all input until dismissed.

    @ref NcursesUi::DialogWidget "DialogWidget" extends PanelWidget to provide
    a ready-made modal dialog with a message, configurable buttons, and
    keyboard navigation (Tab between buttons, Enter to activate).

    Pass the session to the dialog constructor and register callbacks with
    @ref NcursesUi::DialogWidget::setOnButton() "DialogWidget::setOnButton()" and
    @ref NcursesUi::DialogWidget::setOnDismiss() "DialogWidget::setOnDismiss()". The button
    callback receives its index and label. See @ref ncurses_ui_panels "Panel Widgets and Modal Dialogs"
    for a complete example, including modal removal and session cleanup.

    @section ncursesui_widgets Standard Widgets

    @subsection ncursesui_list ListWidget

    @ref NcursesUi::ListWidget "ListWidget" displays a selectable, scrollable
    list of items with keyboard (arrow keys, Enter) and mouse (click, wheel)
    support. It inherits @ref NcursesUi::Widget "Widget" and manages its own scrolling.

    @subsection ncursesui_textinput TextInputWidget

    @ref NcursesUi::TextInputWidget "TextInputWidget" provides single-line
    text editing with cursor movement, selection, and optional command history.

    @subsection ncursesui_scrollable ScrollableWidget

    @ref NcursesUi::ScrollableWidget "ScrollableWidget" wraps a
    @ref NcursesUi::ScrollableContent "ScrollableContent" provider
    (such as @ref NcursesUi::LineListContent "LineListContent") and manages
    the viewport, scroll position, and scrollbar rendering.

    Wrapping is prepared before scrolling, including before the first draw.
    @ref NcursesUi::ScrollableWidget::setCursorLine() "setCursorLine()" takes a
    logical line and an ANSI-free source character offset. The content provider
    maps this position to terminal cells; callers must not convert it to display
    columns first. A newly positioned caret follows the viewport, while manual
    scrolling releases that following behavior until the next cursor update.
    Clearing a cursor releases only that widget's request. Session cursor
    visibility is controlled separately by the application.

    @par Wrapped prompt example
    @code{.py}
NcursesUi::LineListContent content();
content.setWordWrap(True);
content.setLines(("prompt> 日本語",));
NcursesUi::ScrollableWidget output(content);
output.setFrameValues(0, 0, 3, 10);
output.setCursorLine(0, "prompt> 日本語".length());
output.scrollTo(NcursesUi::ScrollDirection::End);
    @endcode

    @ref NcursesUi::LineListContent::sourceToVisual() "sourceToVisual()" and
    @ref NcursesUi::LineListContent::visualToSource() "visualToSource()" share the
    same wrapped rows used for drawing. Word-break whitespace retains its source
    offsets, and positions inside a grapheme snap to its beginning. Horizontal
    scrolling uses display columns and preserves styling; partially visible
    graphemes are represented by spaces. Resizing preserves the source position
    at the top of the viewport when that position still exists.

    @subsection ncursesui_menubar MenuBarWidget

    @ref NcursesUi::MenuBarWidget "MenuBarWidget" renders a horizontal menu
    bar. Each menu item can have an Alt+key hotkey (displayed with an underline
    indicator). Clicking or pressing Alt+key opens a
    @ref NcursesUi::DropdownMenuWidget "DropdownMenuWidget" popup.

    @subsection ncursesui_statusbar StatusBarWidget

    @ref NcursesUi::StatusBarWidget "StatusBarWidget" renders a single-row
    status bar with styled segments. Segments can be left-aligned or
    right-aligned.

    @par StatusBarWidget example:
    @code{.py}
NcursesUi::StatusBarWidget bar();
bar.setSegments((
    {"text": " Ready ", "style": {"fg": Ncurses::Color::Cyan, "bg": Ncurses::Color::Blue}},
    {"text": " Ln 1 ", "style": {"fg": Ncurses::Color::Yellow, "bg": Ncurses::Color::Blue}, "align": "right"},
));
    @endcode

    @subsection ncursesui_dialog DialogWidget

    @ref NcursesUi::DialogWidget "DialogWidget" provides modal dialogs with a
    title, message, and configurable buttons. Supports keyboard navigation
    (Tab to switch buttons, Enter to activate, Escape to cancel).

    @subsection ncursesui_filebrowser FileBrowserWidget

    @ref NcursesUi::FileBrowserWidget "FileBrowserWidget" provides a split-pane
    file system browser with directory listing, file preview, and mouse/keyboard
    navigation including click and scroll wheel support.

    @subsection ncursesui_other Other Widgets

    - @ref NcursesUi::ComboBoxWidget "ComboBoxWidget": dropdown selector
    - @ref NcursesUi::CheckboxWidget "CheckboxWidget": toggle checkbox
    - @ref NcursesUi::RadioGroupWidget "RadioGroupWidget": mutually exclusive radio buttons
    - @ref NcursesUi::TableWidget "TableWidget": column-based data table

    @section ncursesui_testing Testing with TestHarness

    The source-only helper in @c test/TestHarness.qc wraps a
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::TestTerminal "TestTerminal" and @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session "Session"
    to provide a headless testing environment. Include it explicitly from the source checkout;
    it is not installed as part of the toolkit. For application testing, pass its session to
    @ref NcursesUi::Application "Application", as explained in
    @ref ncurses_testingguide "Automated Testing".

    @par TestHarness example:
    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses
%requires NcursesUi
%requires QUnit
%include test/TestHarness.qc

NcursesUi::TestHarness th(24, 80);
on_exit th.close();
th.screen().drawText(0, 0, "Ready");
th.screen().refresh();
@assert(th.screen().readText(0, 0, 5) == "Ready");
th.injectChar("x");
@assert(th.readEvent().ch == "x");
    @endcode

    @section ncursesui_styling Style Conventions

    The \c qrepl application demonstrates a consistent dark theme:
    - Blue backgrounds with cyan, yellow, and white foreground text
    - Menu bar: \c {"fg": Ncurses::Color::Cyan, "bg": Ncurses::Color::Blue}
    - Status bar: same blue background with colored labels
    - Dropdown highlight: \c {"fg": Ncurses::Color::Yellow, "bg": Ncurses::Color::Blue, "attrs": Ncurses::Attr::Bold}
    - Dialog focused button: \c {"fg": Ncurses::Color::Yellow, "bg": Ncurses::Color::Blue, "attrs": Ncurses::Attr::Bold}

    @since ncurses 1.0
*/

#! main namespace for the NcursesUi toolkit
public namespace NcursesUi {

/** Widget geometry rectangle.
    @since ncurses 1.0
*/
public hashdecl Rect {
    #! row position (y)
    int y = 0;
    #! column position (x)
    int x = 0;
    #! number of rows (height)
    int rows = 0;
    #! number of columns (width)
    int cols = 0;
}

/** Padding/margin insets.
    @since ncurses 1.0
*/
public hashdecl Insets {
    #! top inset
    int top = 0;
    #! bottom inset
    int bottom = 0;
    #! left inset
    int left = 0;
    #! right inset
    int right = 0;
}

/** Event handling result.
    @since ncurses 1.0
*/
public hashdecl EventResult {
    #! True if the event was consumed
    bool handled = False;
    #! optional action name (e.g. "ok", "cancel", "close", "select")
    *string action;
    #! optional associated data
    *hash<auto> data;
}

/** @internal A modal scope and the focus suspended while it is active. */
hashdecl ModalFocusState {
    NcursesUi::Widget widget;
    *NcursesUi::Widget previous_focus;
    *NcursesUi::Widget previous_scope;
    bool popup = False;
}

/** Size policy for layout managers.
    @since ncurses 1.0
*/
public enum SizePolicy : int {
    #! widget has a fixed size that does not change
    Fixed = 0,
    #! widget can shrink but prefers its minimum size
    Minimum = 1,
    #! widget prefers its preferred size but can grow or shrink
    Preferred = 2,
    #! widget expands to fill available space
    Expanding = 3,
}

/** Focus traversal direction.
    @since ncurses 1.0
*/
public enum FocusDirection : int {
    #! move to next focusable widget (Tab)
    Next = 0,
    #! move to previous focusable widget (Shift+Tab)
    Previous = 1,
}

/** Layout orientation.
    @since ncurses 1.0
*/
public enum Orientation : int {
    #! horizontal layout (left to right)
    Horizontal = 0,
    #! vertical layout (top to bottom)
    Vertical = 1,
}

/** Scroll direction.
    @since ncurses 1.0
*/
public enum ScrollDirection : int {
    #! scroll up by one line
    Up = 0,
    #! scroll down by one line
    Down = 1,
    #! scroll left by one column
    Left = 2,
    #! scroll right by one column
    Right = 3,
    #! scroll up by one page
    PageUp = 4,
    #! scroll down by one page
    PageDown = 5,
    #! scroll to the beginning
    Home = 6,
    #! scroll to the end
    End = 7,
}

} # namespace NcursesUi
